---
layout: article
title: Actions
description: Learn what the Appwrite Agent can inspect, clarify, and do in your projects and in the Console.
---

The Agent can answer questions from documentation and project context alone. When [MCP](/docs/products/agent/mcp) is connected, it can also call tools and drive Console UI through approved actions.

# Answer and guide {% #answer-and-guide %}

Without tools, the Agent can:

- Explain Appwrite concepts and how-to steps
- Troubleshoot common setup issues
- Suggest next steps for Auth, Databases, Storage, Functions, Sites, and other products
- Use your current Console page as context for more relevant answers

Empty-state suggestions focus on how-to questions until MCP is connected.

# Clarification {% #clarification %}

Before ambiguous or destructive work, the Agent may ask you to:

- **Choose** one or more options from a list
- **Confirm** an action (including higher-risk confirms)
- **Enter text** (single or multiline) to supply missing details

Your answer continues the same turn. You stay in control of anything that changes project data.

# MCP tools {% #mcp-tools %}

With **Appwrite MCP** connected, the Agent can search available tools, call Appwrite APIs with your OAuth scopes, and summarize create, update, delete, and read operations in the conversation.

Typical uses:

- List databases, tables, buckets, users, and other resources
- Create or update resources (for example a todos table with columns)
- Search Appwrite documentation while working in context
- Inspect usage and related project data the tools expose

Action-oriented suggestions appear when an enabled MCP connection can run tools. See [MCP connections](/docs/products/agent/mcp) and [Connect Appwrite MCP](/docs/products/agent/connect-mcp).

# Console UI actions {% #console-ui-actions %}

The Agent can emit Console actions that the UI applies locally. Examples include:

| Action | Effect |
|--------|--------|
| Navigate | Open a Console route (projects, settings, resource pages) |
| Open create | Start create flows for databases, buckets, users, teams, functions, or sites |
| Open dialog | Open system dialogs such as invite member, create project, connect MCP, shortcuts, docs search, feedback, or support |
| Toast | Show success, error, info, or warning notifications |
| Refresh | Refetch lists for databases, tables, buckets, files, users, teams, functions, sites, messaging, project, or organization |
| Theme | Switch light, dark, or system theme |
| Show pane | Open or close the Agent or docs pane |
| Resource cards | Render resource or list cards in chat with deep links |
| Charts | Render usage charts from usage events or gauges in the chat |

These actions help the Agent walk you through the Console and keep lists up to date after mutations.

# TablesDB helpers {% #tablesdb-helpers %}

In TablesDB spreadsheet and workspace views, when the Agent feature is enabled, you may see **Suggest schema** and **Suggest indexes** helpers. Those use the same AI capability to propose columns or indexes for the current table. Write access to the table is still required to apply changes.

# Permissions and safety {% #permissions-and-safety %}

- Agent settings (conversations, models, memory, MCP tokens, automations) are scoped to **your Console user**.
- Live project mutations go through **MCP OAuth** using scopes you grant as **Appwrite Agent**.
- The Agent should ask for clarification before risky or unclear work. Always review proposed changes when you are unsure.

